ENTRY 11814 {"id":11814,"kind":"pi.tool-result","messages":[{"role":"toolResult","text":"packages/orchestrator/src/repo-access.ts:84:    conversationId: number,\npackages/orchestrator/src/repo-access.ts:93:  async beforeUse(conversationId: number): Promise<void> {\npackages/orchestrator/src/repo-access.ts:271:  async revokeSession(sessionId: string): Promise<void> {\npackages/orchestrator/src/watcher.ts:6:  conversationId: number;\npackages/orchestrator/src/watcher.ts:18:  lookup: (conversationId: number, requestId: string) => Promise<SubmissionState | undefined>;\npackages/orchestrator/src/sandboxes.ts:27:export type SessionKeyOf = (conversationId: number) => Promise<string>;\npackages/orchestrator/src/sandboxes.ts:35:  shellEnv?: (conversationId: number) => Promise<Record<string, string> | undefined>;\npackages/orchestrator/src/sandboxes.ts:37:  beforeUse?: (conversationId: number) => Promise<void>;\npackages/orchestrator/src/sandboxes.ts:43:  execInFlight?: (conversationId: number, inFlight: boolean) => Promise<void>;\npackages/orchestrator/src/sandboxes.ts:54:export function claimNameFor(conversationId: number): string {\npackages/orchestrator/src/sandboxes.ts:131:  lazyEnv(conversationId: number): ExecutionEnv {\npackages/orchestrator/src/sandboxes.ts:192:  #settle(conversationId: number, usage: Usage): void {\npackages/orchestrator/src/sandboxes.ts:219:  async #awaitCleanPod(conversationId: number): Promise<void> {\npackages/orchestrator/src/sandboxes.ts:237:    conversationId: number,\npackages/orchestrator/src/sandboxes.ts:271:  async #closeEnv(conversationId: number): Promise<void> {\npackages/orchestrator/src/sandboxes.ts:311:  async ensure(conversationId: number): Promise<SandboxEnv> {\npackages/orchestrator/src/sandboxes.ts:322:  async #open(conversationId: number): Promise<SandboxEnv> {\npackages/orchestrator/src/sandboxes.ts:371:  async destroy(conversationId: number): Promise<void> {\npackages/orchestrator/src/sandboxes.ts:386:  async #teardown(conversationId: number, sessionKey: string): Promise<void> {\npackages/orchestrator/src/main.ts:72:  const sessionKeyOf = async (conversationId: number): Promise<string> => {\npackages/orchestrator/src/main.ts:141:    listSessions: () => listSessionRefs(pool),\npackages/orchestrator/src/main.ts:144:    listOneCli:\npackages/orchestrator/src/main.ts:152:    revokeSession: (sessionId) => repos.revokeSession(sessionId),\npackages/orchestrator/src/sweeper.ts:7:  listSessions: () => Promise<SessionRef[]>;\npackages/orchestrator/src/sweeper.ts:11:  listOneCli: (() => Promise<{ agents: SweepAgent[]; secrets: SweepSecret[] }>) | undefined;\npackages/orchestrator/src/sweeper.ts:14:  revokeSession: (sessionId: string) => Promise<void>;\npackages/orchestrator/src/sweeper.ts:58:        d.listOneCli?.(),\npackages/orchestrator/src/sweeper.ts:96:        return this.#deps.revokeSession(action.sessionId);\npackages/orchestrator/src/stream.ts:119:  conversationId: number,\npackages/orchestrator/src/sessions.ts:111:        conversationId: Number(row.conversation_id),\npackages/orchestrator/src/sessions.ts:152:    conversationId: number | null,\npackages/orchestrator/src/sessions.ts:252:  async #prepareRepo(session: SessionRow, conversationId: number): Promise<void> {\npackages/orchestrator/src/sessions.ts:278:  async #withinBudget(session: SessionRow, conversationId: number): Promise<void> {\n# 0002: Orphan sweep\n\nStatus: accepted, 2026-11-16 (issue #9). Implements the \"periodic sweep\" of the plan's Lifecycle baseline.\n\n## Context\n\nSession deletion removes the claim, the PVC and the OneCLI objects, but a crash, a test that dropped its rows before\nthe delete finished, or a session that was never deleted through the API leaves objects behind. Each is a gVisor Pod\nand a PVC, or a OneCLI agent whose token still works. Nothing reconciled the cluster against `inbox.sessions`.\n\n## Decision\n\nThe orchestrator (the schema owner, so only one process) runs `OrphanSweeper` every `PI_SWEEP_INTERVAL_SECONDS`\n(300; 0 turns it off). Decision and execution are split: `planSweep` (`sweep.ts`) is a pure function from\n`{sessions, claims, PVCs, OneCLI agents and secrets, now}` to a list of actions; `OrphanSweeper` (`sweeper.ts`)\nreads the world, executes the list and logs every action.\n\n**What counts as an orphan.** Only a session that is `deleted` or has no row at all (`session-deleted`,\n`session-unknown`). `active`, `failed` and `deleting` sessions are live.\n\n**What may be swept, by exact pattern only:**\n\n| Object | Pattern | Orphan when |\n|---|---|---|\n| SandboxClaim | name `pi-conv-<n>` and label `pi-durable-k8s/session-id` is a UUID | the label's session is deleted or unknown |\n| PVC | `workspace-pi-conv-<n>` | no claim of that name exists (labelled or not) and the session that owns conversation `<n>` is deleted or unknown |\n| OneCLI agent and secrets | agent `pi-session-<uuid>`, secrets `pi-session-<uuid>-git` and `-api` | that session is deleted or unknown |\n\nEverything else is left alone: unlabelled claims (the e2e Phase 1 claim `e2e-phase1`), `control-<n>` labels of the\ntest-only control sessions, other names, other namespaces. A claim whose PVC is still wanted by another claim name is\nnever touched.\n\n**Safety.**\n\n- *Grace age.* Nothing younger than `PI_SWEEP_GRACE_SECONDS` (600) is swept, from the object's `creationTimestamp`.\n  OneCLI does not report creation times; an agent is judged by its session alone. That is safe because the session row\n  exists before any of its objects does and is never hard-deleted by the API.\n- *Bounded.* At most `PI_SWEEP_MAX_ACTIONS` (10) per run, claims first, then PVCs, then agents. The rest waits.\n- *Logged.* One `sweep-action` line per action (kind, claim or session id, reason), `sweep-action-failed` with the\n  message on error. Names and ids only; no token or secret value is ever in the log (the agent token is not even carried\n  into the action list).\n- *Reuses the delete path.* A claim goes through `Sandboxes.destroyOrphan`, which is the teardown of session deletion\n  (stop the bridge, `deleteClaimAndPvc`). That function still refuses a claim whose label is not the one the sweep\n  read, so a claim that changed hands between listing and deleting survives. A lone PVC goes through the same function\n  with a key no label can equal. OneCLI goes through `RepoAccess.revokeSession`, the by-name revoke that session\n  deletion also uses (agent first, so its token dies first).\n- *Tombstones.* A `deleted` session already has its tombstone from the delete that did not finish. A session with no\n  row has nothing to record; the log line is its trace.\n\n## Not in scope: an active session whose claim can never work again\n\nA claim created under the shared token (before ADR 0001) belongs to an `active` session and fails every call with the\n\"delete the claim and its PVC\" error. The sweep does not remove it. The workspace is the only copy of that session's\nfiles, the session is one the user can still talk to, and ADR 0001 made recreating it an explicit operator decision.\nDeleting the session through `DELETE /sessions/{id}` removes the claim and PVC through the normal path. (This is how the\nleftover test sessions on c2, among them the owners of `pi-conv-5858` and `pi-conv-5873`, were cleaned.)\n\n## Consequences\n\n- The sweep needs `list` on PVCs, in addition to the claim verbs the orchestrator already has (`deploy/orchestrator-rbac.yaml`).\n- A OneCLI shared with another environment that also creates `pi-session-<uuid>` agents would see those agents swept\n  as \"unknown\". c2's OneCLI serves this project only. Do not share one OneCLI between two session databases.\n- A conversation whose session row is hard-deleted by hand (as the e2e cleanup does after deleting through the API) has\n  any leftover claim swept as `session-unknown`, which is the intent.\n","isError":false}]}
ENTRY 11835 {"id":11835,"kind":"pi.assistant","messages":[{"role":"assistant","text":"[thinking]","calls":["bash({\"command\":\"cd /workspace/repo && sed -n '80,180p' packages/orchestrator/src/sessions.ts; sed -n '240,310p' packages/orchestrator/src/repo-access.ts; grep -R -n 'function listSessionRefs\\\\|listSessionRefs' packages; sed -n '120,180p' packages/orchestrator/src/kube.ts; nl -ba packages/orchestrator/src/sweep.ts | sed -n '80,150p'\"})"]}]}
ENTRY 11843 {"id":11843,"kind":"pi.tool-result","messages":[{"role":"toolResult","text":"      onUnanswered: (watched, outcome) => this.#runEnded(watched, outcome),\n      onError: (error) => {\n        log(\"run-watch-failed\", { message: errorMessage(error) });\n      },\n    });\n  }\n\n  stop(): void {\n    this.#watcher.stop();\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * After a start: watch the inputs of live sessions that were handed over recently, because the process that\n   * handed them over may have died before it saw the run fail. Settled ones drop out at the first poll.\n   */\n  async recoverWatches(): Promise<void> {\n    const { rows } = await this.#pool.query<{\n      id: string;\n      session_id: string;\n      conversation_id: string;\n    }>(\n      `select e.id, e.session_id, s.conversation_id\n         from inbox.events e join inbox.sessions s on s.id = e.session_id\n        where e.kind in ('message', 'steer') and e.status = 'submitted'\n          and s.status = 'active' and s.conversation_id is not null\n          and e.submitted_at > clock_timestamp() - interval '24 hours'\n        order by e.submitted_at desc limit 1000`,\n    );\n    for (const row of rows) {\n      this.#watcher.add({\n        sessionId: row.session_id,\n        conversationId: Number(row.conversation_id),\n        requestId: row.id,\n      });\n    }\n    if (rows.length > 0) log(\"run-watches-recovered\", { count: rows.length });\n    await this.#recoverFailedAborts();\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * A session is marked `failed` before its conversation is aborted, so a crash or a storage error in between leaves a\n   * failed session whose queued inputs still run, and nothing watches a failed session. Abort the recently failed\n   * ones again: `abort` is idempotent and a no-op on an idle conversation.\n   */\n  async #recoverFailedAborts(): Promise<void> {\n    const { rows } = await this.#pool.query<{ id: string; conversation_id: string }>(\n      `select id, conversation_id from inbox.sessions\n        where status = 'failed' and conversation_id is not null\n          and last_activity_at > clock_timestamp() - interval '24 hours'\n        order by last_activity_at desc limit 1000`,\n    );\n    for (const row of rows) {\n      try {\n        await this.#host.abort(Number(row.conversation_id));\n      } catch (error) {\n        log(\"failed-session-abort-failed\", { session: row.id, message: errorMessage(error) });\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * A submission ended without an answer. Rejected model credentials and a used-up turn budget end the session\n   * for good (`failed`); anything else leaves it active. The stored message is ours, never the provider's text.\n   */\n  async #runEnded(watched: Watched, outcome: RunOutcome): Promise<void> {\n    const failure = terminalFailure(outcome);\n    if (failure === undefined) return;\n    await this.#failSession(watched.sessionId, watched.conversationId, failure);\n  }\n\n  async #failSession(\n    sessionId: string,\n    conversationId: number | null,\n    failure: string,\n  ): Promise<void> {\n    const changed = await failSession(this.#pool, sessionId, failure);\n    if (changed) {\n      log(\"session-failed\", { session: sessionId, failure });\n    } else if ((await getSession(this.#pool, sessionId))?.status !== \"failed\") {\n      return;\n    }\n    // Withdraw whatever queued behind the failed run, so nothing more is sent to the provider. Also when the session\n    // was failed already: the status commits before the abort, so a caller whose abort died (or whose process did)\n    // retries here and must not find \"nothing changed\" and stop. A deleting or deleted session is not ours to abort.\n    if (conversationId !== null) await this.#host.abort(conversationId);\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * The session's conversation id, creating the conversation on first use. Serialised per session, so the\n   * stream handler and the inbox loop cannot create two. A crash between creating the conversation and\n   * storing its id leaves one empty, unreferenced conversation behind (documented limit).\n   */\n  async ensureConversation(session: SessionRow): Promise<number> {\n    if (session.conversationId !== null) return session.conversationId;\n    let creating = this.#creating.get(session.id);\n    if (creating === undefined) {\n      creating = this.#create(session.id).finally(() => this.#creating.delete(session.id));\n      this.#creating.set(session.id, creating);\n    }\n    return creating;\n  }\n    });\n    await markWorkspaceReady(this.#deps.pool, session.id);\n    this.#prepared.add(session.id);\n    // `workspace-cloned` once per session; `workspace-present` after a restart. tests/e2e/run-phase4c.sh greps both.\n    log(outcome === \"cloned\" ? \"workspace-cloned\" : \"workspace-present\", {\n      session: session.id,\n      repo: spec.repo,\n    });\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Revokes everything the session held in OneCLI: the agent first (its token fails at once), then the secrets.\n   * Looks objects up by name as well as by stored id, so a crash between creating an object and storing its id\n   * cannot leave one behind. Idempotent. A plain session has nothing and makes no OneCLI call.\n   */\n  async teardown(session: SessionRow): Promise<void> {\n    if (session.repo === null) return;\n    const { onecli } = this.#deps;\n    this.#forget(session.id);\n    if (onecli === undefined) {\n      if (session.onecli === null) return;\n      throw new Error(\"cannot revoke the session's OneCLI agent: ONECLI_API_KEY is not set\");\n    }\n    await this.#revoke(session.id, session.onecli?.agentId, session.onecli?.secretIds ?? []);\n    log(\"repo-access-revoked\", { session: session.id });\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * The orphan sweep's revoke: removes whatever OneCLI still holds under this session's names (agent first, then the\n   * secrets), with no session row needed. Nothing is stored for a session that is deleted or unknown.\n   */\n  async revokeSession(sessionId: string): Promise<void> {\n    this.#forget(sessionId);\n    await this.#revoke(sessionId, undefined, []);\n  }\n\n  async #revoke(\n    sessionId: string,\n    agentId: string | undefined,\n    secretIds: readonly string[],\n  ): Promise<void> {\n    const { onecli } = this.#deps;\n    if (onecli === undefined) return;\n    const agents = (await onecli.listAgents())\n      .filter((a) => a.identifier === agentIdentifier(sessionId))\n      .map((a) => a.id);\n    for (const id of new Set([...(agentId === undefined ? [] : [agentId]), ...agents])) {\n      await onecli.deleteAgent(id);\n    }\n    const names = new Set(SECRET_SUFFIXES.map((s) => secretName(sessionId, s.suffix)));\n    const named = (await onecli.listSecrets()).filter((s) => names.has(s.name)).map((s) => s.id);\n    for (const id of new Set([...secretIds, ...named])) {\n      try {\n        await onecli.deleteSecret(id);\n      } catch (error) {\n        if (!(error instanceof OneCliError && error.status === 404)) throw error;\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  #forget(sessionId: string): void {\n    this.#access.delete(sessionId);\n    this.#prepared.delete(sessionId);\n    for (const [conversationId, session] of this.#byConversation) {\n      if (session.id === sessionId) this.#byConversation.delete(conversationId);\n    }\n  }\n}\npackages/session-core/src/store.ts:376:export async function listSessionRefs(db: Pick<pg.Pool, \"query\">): Promise<SessionRef[]> {\npackages/session-core/src/index.ts:27:  listSessionRefs,\npackages/orchestrator/src/main.ts:7:  listSessionRefs,\npackages/orchestrator/src/main.ts:141:    listSessions: () => listSessionRefs(pool),\n * persistentvolumeclaims in the namespace (and the `get` on claims the orchestrator has anyway).\n */\nexport async function deleteClaimAndPvc(\n  namespace: string,\n  claimName: string,\n  sessionKey: string,\n  timeoutMs = 180_000,\n): Promise<void> {\n  const kc = new KubeConfig();\n  kc.loadFromDefault();\n  const custom = kc.makeApiClient(CustomObjectsApi);\n  const core = kc.makeApiClient(CoreV1Api);\n  const claim = {\n    group: \"extensions.agents.x-k8s.io\",\n    version: \"v1beta1\",\n    namespace,\n    plural: \"sandboxclaims\",\n    name: claimName,\n  };\n  // The Sandbox controller names the PVC after the volume claim template and the Sandbox (`workspace-<claim>`).\n  const pvc = { name: `workspace-${claimName}`, namespace };\n\n  // Never delete a claim that is not this session's (`get` is already granted for the SDK).\n  try {\n    const found: unknown = await custom.getNamespacedCustomObject(claim);\n    if (labelOf(found) !== sessionKey) {\n      throw new Error(\n        `SandboxClaim ${claimName} is not labelled for this session: not deleting it`,\n      );\n    }\n  } catch (error) {\n    if (statusOf(error) !== 404) throw error;\n  }\n  // Only `delete` is needed: a delete that answers 404 means the object is gone. The PVC is deleted only once\n  // the claim is gone, so the Sandbox controller cannot recreate it from a Sandbox that still exists.\n  const deadline = Date.now() + timeoutMs;\n  for (;;) {\n    const claimPresent = await ignoreNotFound(custom.deleteNamespacedCustomObject(claim));\n    const pvcPresent = claimPresent\n      ? true\n      : await ignoreNotFound(core.deleteNamespacedPersistentVolumeClaim(pvc));\n    if (!claimPresent && !pvcPresent) return;\n    if (Date.now() > deadline) {\n      throw new Error(\n        `timed out deleting ${claimName}: claim ${claimPresent ? \"present\" : \"gone\"}, pvc ${pvcPresent ? \"present\" : \"gone\"}`,\n      );\n    }\n    await sleep(2_000);\n  }\n}\n\nfunction clients(): { custom: CustomObjectsApi; core: CoreV1Api } {\n  const kc = new KubeConfig();\n  kc.loadFromDefault();\n  return { custom: kc.makeApiClient(CustomObjectsApi), core: kc.makeApiClient(CoreV1Api) };\n}\n\nconst SANDBOX_REF = { group: \"agents.x-k8s.io\", version: \"v1beta1\", plural: \"sandboxes\" };\n\n/** A SandboxClaim as the orphan sweep sees it. `sessionLabel` is undefined for a claim we never labelled. */\nexport interface ClaimInfo {\n    80\t  const bySession = new Map(input.sessions.map((s) => [s.id, s]));\n    81\t  const byConversation = new Map(\n    82\t    input.sessions.flatMap((s) => (s.conversationId === null ? [] : [[s.conversationId, s]])),\n    83\t  );\n    84\t  const old = (createdAt: Date | undefined): boolean =>\n    85\t    createdAt === undefined || input.now - createdAt.getTime() >= input.graceMs;\n    86\t  /** The reason a session no longer owns anything, or undefined if it is live. */\n    87\t  const orphanReason = (session: SessionRef | undefined): SweepReason | undefined => {\n    88\t    if (session === undefined) return \"session-unknown\";\n    89\t    return session.status === \"deleted\" ? \"session-deleted\" : undefined;\n    90\t  };\n    91\t\n    92\t  const actions: SweepAction[] = [];\n    93\t\n    94\t  for (const claim of input.claims) {\n    95\t    if (!CLAIM_NAME.test(claim.name)) continue;\n    96\t    const label = claim.sessionLabel;\n    97\t    if (label === undefined || !UUID.test(label)) continue;\n    98\t    if (!old(claim.createdAt)) continue;\n    99\t    const reason = orphanReason(bySession.get(label));\n   100\t    if (reason !== undefined)\n   101\t      actions.push({ kind: \"delete-claim\", claim: claim.name, sessionLabel: label, reason });\n   102\t  }\n   103\t\n   104\t  // Any claim of that name, labelled or not, means the PVC is (or may soon be) in use: leave it.\n   105\t  const claimNames = new Set(input.claims.map((c) => c.name));\n   106\t  for (const pvc of input.pvcs) {\n   107\t    const match = PVC_NAME.exec(pvc.name);\n   108\t    if (match === null || !old(pvc.createdAt)) continue;\n   109\t    const [, claim, conversation] = match;\n   110\t    if (claim === undefined || conversation === undefined || claimNames.has(claim)) continue;\n   111\t    const reason = orphanReason(byConversation.get(Number(conversation)));\n   112\t    if (reason !== undefined) actions.push({ kind: \"delete-pvc\", claim, reason });\n   113\t  }\n   114\t\n   115\t  if (input.agents !== undefined) {\n   116\t    const found = new Map<string, { agentIds: string[]; secretIds: string[] }>();\n   117\t    const entry = (sessionId: string) => {\n   118\t      let e = found.get(sessionId);\n   119\t      if (e === undefined) {\n   120\t        e = { agentIds: [], secretIds: [] };\n   121\t        found.set(sessionId, e);\n   122\t      }\n   123\t      return e;\n   124\t    };\n   125\t    for (const agent of input.agents) {\n   126\t      const sessionId = AGENT_IDENTIFIER.exec(agent.identifier)?.[1];\n   127\t      if (sessionId === undefined || !old(agent.createdAt)) continue;\n   128\t      if (orphanReason(bySession.get(sessionId)) !== undefined)\n   129\t        entry(sessionId).agentIds.push(agent.id);\n   130\t    }\n   131\t    for (const secret of input.secrets) {\n   132\t      const sessionId = SECRET_NAME.exec(secret.name)?.[1];\n   133\t      if (sessionId === undefined) continue;\n   134\t      if (orphanReason(bySession.get(sessionId)) !== undefined)\n   135\t        entry(sessionId).secretIds.push(secret.id);\n   136\t    }\n   137\t    for (const [sessionId, ids] of found) {\n   138\t      const reason = orphanReason(bySession.get(sessionId));\n   139\t      if (reason !== undefined) actions.push({ kind: \"revoke-agent\", sessionId, ...ids, reason });\n   140\t    }\n   141\t  }\n   142\t\n   143\t  return actions.slice(0, Math.max(0, input.maxActions));\n   144\t}\n","isError":false}]}
ENTRY 11879 {"id":11879,"kind":"pi.assistant","messages":[{"role":"assistant","text":"[thinking]## Findings\n\n### 1. A stale session snapshot can cause a live session’s credentials to be revoked\n- Severity: high\n- Confidence: high\n- Location: packages/orchestrator/src/sweep.ts:131\n- What happens: The sweeper lists sessions and OneCLI objects concurrently. If the session query finishes before a new session is created but the OneCLI listing sees its newly created secret, the planner treats the session as unknown and schedules revocation. Execution revokes the session’s agent and secrets by name, breaking the live session. The same race applies to an agent with no creation timestamp.\n- Evidence: `if (orphanReason(bySession.get(sessionId)) !== undefined) entry(sessionId).secretIds.push(secret.id);`\n- Fix idea: Recheck session ownership against the database immediately before revocation. Also apply a grace period to OneCLI objects where creation timestamps are available, including secrets.\n\n### 2. Repeatedly failing actions can starve the rest of the sweep\n- Severity: medium\n- Confidence: high\n- Location: packages/orchestrator/src/sweep.ts:143\n- What happens: If the first `maxActions` candidates consistently fail deletion—for example, because Kubernetes denies access—the same candidates can occupy every run’s action budget. Later orphan PVCs and agents are never attempted, leaving resources and potentially valid agent tokens behind indefinitely.\n- Evidence: `return actions.slice(0, Math.max(0, input.maxActions));`\n- Fix idea: Rotate or otherwise track candidate ordering across runs, or apply the success limit while allowing later candidates to be attempted after failures.\n\nEND-OF-REPORT"}]}
DONE
